---
import Layout from "../../Base.astro";
import SimpleHero from "../../components/SimpleHero.astro";
import { Picture } from "astro:assets";
import photoAirplane from "../../assets/images/photography/airplane-photography.jpg";
import photoApparel from "../../assets/images/photography/apparal-photography.jpg";
import photoExterior from "../../assets/images/photography/exterior-building-photography.jpg";
import photoFood from "../../assets/images/photography/food-business-photography.jpg";
import photoLaw from "../../assets/images/photography/law-firm-photography.jpg";
import photoTraining from "../../assets/images/photography/training-photography.jpg";
import photoWell from "../../assets/images/photography/well-drilling-photography.jpg";
import FeaturedArticles from "../../components/FeaturedArticles.astro";
import ServicesRelatedWork from "../../components/ServicesRelatedWork.astro";
import "../../styles/pages/_services-list.scss";
---

<Layout
  title="Brand, Product &amp; Website Photography | Kelp"
  description="Photography planned for the pages and campaigns where customers make decisions, from products and people to places and events."
>
  <SimpleHero
    tagline="Content Creation Services"
    title="Photography"
    description="When people meet your brand online first, weak photography creates doubt before you get a chance to speak. We create photo libraries that make your business look credible, current, and worth engaging."
    lottieFile="photography.json"
  />
  <div
    class="wrapper our-photos"
    data-lg-reveal="layer-to-right"
    data-lg-reveal-stagger="0.1"
  >
    <h2>
      We Take
      <br />
      Photos Like...
    </h2>
    <Picture
      width={1140}
      height={722}
      src={photoAirplane}
      loading="lazy"
      alt="airplane photography"
      widths={[480, 800, 1140]}
      sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 50vw"
      inferSize
    />
    <Picture
      width={1140}
      height={722}
      src={photoApparel}
      loading="lazy"
      alt="apparel photography"
      widths={[480, 800, 1140]}
      sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 50vw"
      inferSize
    />
    <Picture
      width={1140}
      height={722}
      src={photoExterior}
      loading="lazy"
      alt="exterior buildings photography"
      widths={[480, 800, 1140]}
      sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 50vw"
      inferSize
    />
    <Picture
      width={1140}
      height={722}
      src={photoFood}
      loading="lazy"
      alt="food photography"
      widths={[480, 800, 1140]}
      sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 50vw"
      inferSize
    />
    <Picture
      width={1140}
      height={722}
      src={photoLaw}
      loading="lazy"
      alt="law firm photography"
      widths={[480, 800, 1140]}
      sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 50vw"
      inferSize
    />
    <Picture
      width={1140}
      height={722}
      src={photoTraining}
      loading="lazy"
      alt="school training photography"
      widths={[480, 800, 1140]}
      sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 50vw"
      inferSize
    />
    <Picture
      width={1140}
      height={724}
      src={photoWell}
      loading="lazy"
      alt="well drilling photography"
      widths={[480, 800, 1140]}
      sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 50vw"
      inferSize
    />
  </div>
  <div class="service-body">
    <div class="wrapper wrapper--narrow" data-lg-reveal>
      <h2>Where teams get stuck</h2>
      <p>
        A lot of brands rely on old images, inconsistent phone photos, or stock
        photography that does not reflect the actual business. That gap shows up
        fast on websites, social content, sales material, and product pages.
      </p>
      <p>
        When the visuals feel generic or outdated, trust drops before the
        message even has a chance to work.
      </p>
      <h2>How we fix it</h2>
      <p>
        We plan photography around the real places the images need to perform:
        your website, campaigns, product pages, social channels, or internal
        marketing library. That gives the shoot direction before cameras ever
        come out.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Product photography</li>
        <li>Events</li>
        <li>Website</li>
        <li>Social Media</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Build a Useful Shot List</h2>
      <p>
        We identify the questions the imagery should answer, the formats each
        channel needs, and the moments worth capturing. That may mean products
        in use, staff at work, a location, a process, or details that make the
        offer credible. The goal is a reusable library, not a folder of images
        without a plan.
      </p>
      <h2>Make the Site More Specific</h2>
      <p>
        Original imagery can help a custom site reflect the real business. It
        should support accurate product and service information, especially when
        customers may arrive through search or AI answers and need to confirm
        what they found. Plan a shoot with Kelp.
      </p>
      <h2>How This Works in Practice</h2>
      <p>
        The shot list should come from the questions the site and campaign need
        to answer. That may include the people behind a service, the details of
        a product, the environment where work happens, and images that show
        scale or use. Planning locations, permissions, formats, and cropping
        needs ahead of time makes the resulting library more useful across page
        templates and channels.
      </p>
      <h2>What the Work Includes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Brand and team photography</li>
        <li>Product and detail imagery</li>
        <li>Location, event, and process coverage</li>
        <li>Channel-ready selects and usage guidance</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What Moving Forward Looks Like</h2>
      <p>
        Show us the pages and campaigns the images must support. We can turn
        those requirements into a shot plan and a practical production schedule.
      </p>
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <h3>Can you create images for an ecommerce catalog?</h3>
      <p>
        Yes, when the product, volume, styling, and output needs are clear. We
        would scope the shoot around the catalog and its maintenance plan.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="button button--green">
          Plan Your Photo Shoot
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <ServicesRelatedWork tag={68} />
  </div>
  <FeaturedArticles />
</Layout>

<style lang="scss" is:global>
  .our-photos {
    margin-bottom: 6rem;
    column-count: 2;
    column-gap: 3rem;
    @media (max-width: 767px) {
      column-count: 1;
    }
    h2 {
      margin-bottom: 4rem;
    }
    picture {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }
  }
</style>
